# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .assetsignore  —  Cloudflare Workers static-assets ignore list
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lives at the ROOT of the static-assets directory.
#   wrangler.jsonc -> assets.directory = "./dist"
# Astro copies this file from ./public into ./dist on every build, so it is
# always present in the directory Wrangler actually uploads.
#
# Format is identical to .gitignore. Wrangler will NOT upload anything that
# matches a line here as a client-side static asset.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# Wrangler's design choice is to ignore almost NOTHING by default (only
# `_redirects` and `_headers` are special-cased). Without this file, every
# single file in ./dist is pushed to the edge as a public asset — including
# the server-side Worker bundle (`dist/_worker.js/index.js`), which would then
# be publicly downloadable. This file keeps the asset upload limited to the
# real client-side files only: index.html, models/**, textures/**.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Server-side Worker bundle + generated routing config (never serve) ---
_worker.js
_worker.js/**
_routes.json

# --- The ignore file itself ---
.assetsignore

# --- Wrangler / Cloudflare local state & secrets ---
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example
wrangler.json
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml

# --- Dependencies & build tooling (never serve) ---
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.astro/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.map

# --- Project source & repo config (never serve) ---
src/
public/
astro.config.mjs
astro.config.ts
tsconfig.json
package.json
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
README.md
PRD_AND_ARCHITECTURE.md
LICENSE
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.git/
.github/

# --- Editor / OS junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
npm-debug.log*
